          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "てんき (tenki) is Sino-Japanese (kango): two Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese. They are ten, \"heaven, sky\" (Middle Chinese then) and ki, \"air, breath\" (khj+jH) (KANJIDIC2; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
